-- title:
--   Index scaling between lattice and integral-determinant order
-- statement:
--   Fix number fields $K \subseteq L$ with $\operatorname{finrank}_K L = 2$ (`h2`) and $\sigma \in \operatorname{Aut}_K(L)$ such that every $\tau \in \operatorname{Aut}_K(L)$ lies in the subgroup of integer powers of $\sigma$ (`hgen`). Fix $\delta_0 \in \mathrm{GL}_2(L)$, a unit $c$ of $L \otimes_K \mathbf{A}_K$ (where $\mathbf{A}_K$ is the adele ring of $K$) and a unit $u$ of $\mathbf{A}_K$, and write $\delta := \mathrm{GL}_2(\iota_L)(\delta_0)\cdot \mathrm{scalar}(c)$, the image of $\delta_0$ under the inclusion $\iota_L : L \to L \otimes_K \mathbf{A}_K$ times the central scalar matrix $c$.
--
--   The hypotheses on the pair $(\delta,\delta_0)$ are: `hN`, which requires that the norm string $\prod_{i=0}^{[L:K]-1} \sigma_{\mathrm{GL}}^{i}(\delta)$ of $\delta$ (the product over $i \in \{0,\dots,\operatorname{finrank}_K L - 1\}$ of the $i$-th iterate of the map induced by $\sigma \otimes \mathrm{id}$ applied to $\delta$) equals the image of the central scalar matrix $u$ under $\mathrm{GL}_2(\mathbf{A}_K) \to \mathrm{GL}_2(L\otimes_K \mathbf{A}_K)$ induced by $a \mapsto 1 \otimes a$; and `hns`, which requires that for all $x \in \mathrm{GL}_2(L)$ and all $z \in L^\times$ one has $x^{-1}\delta_0\,\sigma(x) \neq \mathrm{scalar}(z)$, i.e. $\delta_0$ is not $\sigma$-conjugate over $L$ to a central scalar.
--
--   Fix a height-one prime $v$ of $\mathcal{O}_K$, write $K_v$ for the $v$-adic completion and $\mathcal{O}_v$ for its ring of integers, and let $\delta_v$ be the image of $\delta$ under the map $\mathrm{GL}_2(L\otimes_K\mathbf{A}_K) \to \mathrm{GL}_2(L\otimes_K K_v)$ induced by $\mathrm{id}_L \otimes (\mathbf{A}_K \to K_v)$. Let $T_v := \{t \in \mathrm{GL}_2(L\otimes_K K_v) : t\,\delta_v\,(\sigma_{\mathrm{GL}}t)^{-1} = \delta_v\}$ be the twisted centraliser of $\delta_v$, carrying its Borel structure, and let $\tau$ be a measure on $T_v$ which is a Haar measure (`hτ`). Let $tv \in [0,\infty]$.
--
--   Two further local hypotheses are imposed. `hnsc`: for no unit $z$ of $L \otimes_K K_v$ is $\mathrm{scalar}(z)$ of the form $x^{-1}\delta_v\,\sigma_{\mathrm{GL}}(x)$ with $x \in \mathrm{GL}_2(L\otimes_K K_v)$, i.e. $\delta_v$ is not $\sigma$-conjugate to a central scalar. `hshell`: writing $S$ for the set of $t \in T_v$ for which there exists $s \in K_v^\times$ with $\mathrm{val}_v(s) = 1$ and $\det t =$ the image of $s$ under the unit map of $a \mapsto 1 \otimes a$, one has $\tau(S)\cdot \#(\mathcal{O}_K/v) = tv + \tau(S)$, where $\#(\mathcal{O}_K/v)$ is the absolute norm of the ideal $v$ viewed in $[0,\infty]$.
--
--   Finally, fix a finite index type $\iota$ and a family $b : \iota \to M_2(L)$ which is $K$-linearly independent (`hb`) and spans the twisted commutant of $\delta_0$ in the sense of `hbspan`: for every $X \in M_2(L)$ one has $X\delta_0 = \delta_0\, X^{\sigma}$ (entrywise application of $\sigma$) if and only if $X$ lies in the $K$-span of the range of $b$.
--
--   Two additive subgroups of $M_2(L\otimes_K K_v)$ enter the conclusion:
--   $$S_\Lambda := \langle\, (b\,i)^{(l \mapsto l \otimes a)} \;:\; i \in \iota,\ a \in \mathcal{O}_v \,\rangle,$$
--   the additive subgroup generated by the entrywise scalings of the basis matrices $b\,i$ by integral elements $a$, and
--   $$S_M := \langle\, X \;:\; X\,\delta_0' = \delta_0'\, X^{\sigma \otimes \mathrm{id}},\ \exists a \in \mathcal{O}_v,\ \det X = 1 \otimes a \,\rangle,$$
--   the additive subgroup generated by those $X$ lying in the twisted commutant of $\delta_0' := \mathrm{GL}_2(L \to L\otimes_K K_v)(\delta_0)$ (no scalar factor $c$ here) whose determinant is of the form $1 \otimes a$ with $a$ integral. Here `relIndex` of one additive subgroup relative to another is the index of their intersection inside the second.
--
--   The conclusion is the conjunction of three assertions.
--
--   First, $S_\Lambda.\mathrm{relIndex}\,S_M \neq 0$, that is, $[S_M : S_\Lambda \cap S_M]$ is finite.
--
--   Second, $S_M.\mathrm{relIndex}\,S_\Lambda \neq 0$, that is, $[S_\Lambda : S_M \cap S_\Lambda]$ is finite.
--
--   Third, the identity
--   $$\Big(\int^-_{\{t \in T_v \,:\, \exists a : \iota \to \mathcal{O}_v,\ t = \sum_k (b\,k)^{(l \mapsto l \otimes a_k)}\}} \mathrm{ofReal}\,\big\|N_{(L\otimes_K K_v)/K_v}(\det t)\big\|\, d\tau\Big)\cdot [S_M : S_\Lambda \cap S_M]$$
--   $$= \Big(\int^-_{\{t \in T_v \,:\, t \in S_M\}} \mathrm{ofReal}\,\big\|N_{(L\otimes_K K_v)/K_v}(\det t)\big\|\, d\tau\Big)\cdot [S_\Lambda : S_M \cap S_\Lambda],$$
--   where in both lower integrals $t$ is identified with its underlying matrix in $M_2(L\otimes_K K_v)$, the first region consists of those $t \in T_v$ whose matrix is an $\mathcal{O}_v$-integral combination $\sum_k (b\,k)^{(l \mapsto l \otimes a_k)}$ of the basis matrices with all $a_k \in \mathcal{O}_v$, the second of those $t \in T_v$ whose matrix lies in the underlying set of $S_M$, and the integrand is the extended-real value of the absolute value of the $K_v$-algebra norm of $\det t$.
--
--   This is the index-scaling comparison between the $\mathcal{O}_v$-lattice spanned by a $K$-basis of the twisted commutant of $\delta_0$ and the order cut out inside that commutant by integrality of the determinant: the two twisted orbital integrals of $\|N\det\|_v$ over these two regions differ exactly by the ratio of the two relative indices, both of which are finite. It feeds the local covolume computation in [`AutomorphicForm.setLIntegral_lattice_norm_det_mul_norm_four_eq_mul_sqrt_norm_det_trace_of_not_isSigmaConjugate_scalar`](thm.html#AutomorphicForm.setLIntegral_lattice_norm_det_mul_norm_four_eq_mul_sqrt_norm_det_trace_of_not_isSigmaConjugate_scalar), for a place $v$ at which $\delta_v$ is not $\sigma$-conjugate to a central scalar.
